  "$comment": "ENH-052 family 5 input matrix — the push-schema validation rule rows the generator (server/src/spec_corpus_validation.rs) runs through the server's own SchemaDef::validate to compute wire-corpus/spec/validation.json. Hand-maintained, one row per representative per rule the wire outcome distinguishes; each reject row violates exactly one rule so cascade ordering never changes the outcome. Reject codes: index/ttl/updated-at/auto-increment/on-delete/constraints rules reject as SCHEMA_VIOLATION, computed rules as BAD_REQUEST. Deliberately EXCLUDED (see wire-corpus/README.md 'Spec-table corpus'): rules the existing semantics corpus already pins (authorize olderThan, partial-index where olderThan, computed undeclared-reference, computed static-kind string-to-number, computed case-when principal markers, constraints invalid-regex, constraints min-on-string-field) and rules that stay server-side (identifier formats, case-collision, owner/collaborators field type rules, defaults validation, vector-spec deep rules, search-language placement/format, trgm placement — the in-memory engines deliberately mirror a subset).",
